    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Yes, exertion. That makes it worse. It happens once or twice a day. Maybe a eight out of ten on a bad day. I took the morning off to come in today. As for swollen ankles, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before. Uh, as for swollen ankles, I'd say once or twice a day. I did have chest tightness at one point, uh, but that's gone now.",
