      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "speaker_role": "nurse",
      "transcript_text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Pulse is 91 beats a minute, BP is 129 over 81, temperature is 36.8 degrees.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:48",
      "end_timestamp": "02:56",
      "supports": [
        "vital_signs[0]",
        "vital_signs[1]",
        "vital_signs[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "There is a loud second heart sound and a raised jugular pulse.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:24",
      "end_timestamp": "03:30",
      "supports": [
        "physical_examination[0]",
        "physical_examination[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "good, you can sit up again. Let me tell you where I've got to. It points towards possible pulmonary hypertension. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together",
      "start_timestamp": "03:32",
      "end_timestamp": "03:48",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with possible pulmonary hypertension do well once it's treated properly. I'm sending you for an ECG because of syncope. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. Let's get an echocardiogram, for exertional syncope. No exertion for now, I am arranging urgent specialist tests. I think the pulmonary hypertension service should see you too.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:52",
      "end_timestamp": "04:19",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]",
        "procedures_and_investigations[0]",
